# ICU: Qt only uses it for extended QStringConverter codecs, QCollator
# collation and localised timezone display names. rpi-imager uses none of
# these (UTF-8 only, no collation, timezones handled as IANA ID strings), and
# Qt has non-ICU fallbacks for all three. Excluding it drops ~35 MB of
# libicudata/libicui18n/libicuuc per package and removes the per-release
# soname pin (libicu72 on bookworm, libicu76 on trixie).
icu
